{"id":"chatcmpl-00634f09-bf6d-493f-b47f-1d5b2d6bc3b1","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246645,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task shows a multi-tool consensus strategy for medical image QA where the key challenge is resolving conflicting tool outputs and handling laterality ambiguity on a lateral view. The successful approach queried multiple independent vision models with targeted anatomical questions, then used a verification step to audit conflicts before committing to the sole positive side-specific finding. The pattern generalizes to any task where multiple imperfect experts must be reconciled under inherent ambiguity.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Query multiple independent expert tools with the same targeted anatomical question to surface consensus vs. outlier signals before answering.\",\n    \"When the imaging view makes the answer dimension (e.g., laterality) inherently ambiguous, explicitly flag that limitation and rely on the sole positive side-specific finding rather than forcing consensus.\",\n    \"Use a verification/audit step to explicitly weigh conflicting tool outputs and document the risk before finalizing, rather than silently picking one.\",\n    \"Decompose the question into presence-detection first, then location/laterality mapping, so each tool call targets one sub-decision.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image QA with multiple VLM tools\": \"Ask each tool the same focused anatomical question; treat agreement as strong signal and a lone positive as a candidate requiring audit.\",\n    \"Ambiguous-view laterality tasks\": \"Acknowledge view limitations explicitly; prefer the only side-specific positive finding over 'no finding' consensus when options force a side.\",\n    \"Conflicting expert outputs\": \"Insert a verify step that states the conflict and risk, then justify the final choice by which tool gave the discriminating signal.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before answering: confirm whether tools agree on presence, and identify any lone positive that discriminates between options.\",\n    \"Before finalizing: run a verify/audit step documenting conflicts and view-based ambiguity, then justify the selected option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":778,"total_tokens":1169,"completion_tokens":391,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":778},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":391}}}